# Engine image builds use this repository root as their context. Build output
# and vendored data stay outside the context.
#
# The rule is therefore inverted - everything is excluded, and the few trees
# the engine build reads are named back in. A directory added later is outside
# the context until someone deliberately lists it, which is the safe direction:
# the failure mode is a build that cannot find a file, not an image that
# silently ships one.
*

!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!.cargo
!crates
!scripts
!tools

# fq-index keeps its own workspace, its own lock and its own target directory
# (gigabytes of rust-analyzer artifacts). The engine build never reads it.
tools/fq-index
